      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so the French were basically saying the Viet Minh's whole independence movement was illegitimate because of their ideology and the French Union. looking back at the history, does it seem like the French had any real moral or legal ground for that, or was it just a way to keep their grip on the region despite the local opposition?",
